# Why OpenRouter is unused despite being keyed (tested 2026-07-29):
#
# All three wowlidator roles go through generateObject — schema-constrained JSON is
# the framework's hard requirement, not a preference. This key is free-tier
# (is_free_tier=true, no credits), so only the 14 `:free` models are reachable,
# and only 4 of those advertise structured_outputs. All 4 were tested against
# the real agent decision schema on localhost:3000, and all 4 failed:
#
#   openai/gpt-oss-20b:free               returned nothing at all (0 out tokens)
#   google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it:free        responded, did not match schema
#   nvidia/nemotron-nano-9b-v2:free       spent 1163 tokens reasoning, unparseable
#   nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free  unparseable
#
# gpt-oss-20b was also tried on the simpler healer schema — same failure. The
# identical flows pass on Gemini, so this is model capability, not wowlidator.
#
# To actually use this key: add credits so non-free models become reachable,
# then point a role at a small paid model. Re-check with `npm run cli -- doctor`
# plus one real run — doctor only proves the id resolves, not that the model can
# emit schema-constrained JSON.

# --- Role routing ----------------------------------------------------------
# Google + OpenRouter are keyed; Groq is not. The agent now runs on OpenRouter
# so it no longer shares Google's free-tier request bucket with the generator —
# a throttled agent can't stall generation, and vice versa.
#
# Move the healer to Groq once GROQ_API_KEY exists; that is its intended home
# (repair is latency-sensitive and Groq is the fastest of the three).

# Repair is small and latency-sensitive: use the cheapest, fastest flash tier.
# WOWLIDATOR_HEALER_PROVIDER=google
# WOWLIDATOR_HEALER_MODEL=antigravity-preview-05-2026

# Generation sends the largest prompt in the system (a whole AX tree).
# WOWLIDATOR_GENERATOR_PROVIDER=google
# WOWLIDATOR_GENERATOR_MODEL=antigravity-preview-05-2026

# Navigation is turn-by-turn reasoning over the AX tree.
#
# On a DIFFERENT model from the generator on purpose: Google's free tier meters
# per model id, so this gives the agent its own request bucket and a throttled
# generator can no longer stall navigation. gemini-3.6-flash also works here and
# is ~2x faster (26s vs 50s on a 6-turn navigation) — switch if you would rather
# have the speed than the separate bucket.
# WOWLIDATOR_AGENT_PROVIDER=google
# WOWLIDATOR_AGENT_MODEL=antigravity-preview-05-2026

# Free tiers throttle hard; the SDK backs off between attempts.
WOWLIDATOR_LLM_MAX_RETRIES=3

# --- Output location -------------------------------------------------------
# Everything wowlidator produces lands in the workspace root (/ai-val), one level
# above the package, so artifacts aren't mixed in with source.
#
# Absolute paths on purpose: relative ones resolve against the *current working
# directory*, so `cd wowlidator && wowlidator run` and `wowlidator run` from the root would
# otherwise write to two different places.
WOWLIDATOR_REPORT_DIR=/Users/ThArus/Documents/workspace/ai-val/valst-output/reports
WOWLIDATOR_PROOF_DIR=/Users/ThArus/Documents/workspace/ai-val/valst-output/proofs
WOWLIDATOR_CACHE_PATH=/Users/ThArus/Documents/workspace/ai-val/valst-output/healed-selectors.json

# --- Browser ---------------------------------------------------------------
# No window. Launching Chrome with no URL opens chrome://newtab — Google's
# search box and its one-google-bar iframe — and on this persistent profile
# they accumulated: five of them by the time anyone counted. Runs are the same
# either way; screenshots, the accessibility tree and the filmstrip all work
# headless. Pass --no-headless on a single command when you want to watch one.
WOWLIDATOR_HEADLESS=1

